1
00:00:00,371 --> 00:00:01,401
(Howard:)without sounding
so condescending?

2
00:00:01,406 --> 00:00:03,836
(Leonard:)I can try, but your
plan has the words

3
00:00:03,842 --> 00:00:05,842
"garbage bag" and
"Slim Jim" in it!

4
00:00:05,844 --> 00:00:08,244
(Raj:)Hey, what's going on?
Oh.

5
00:00:08,246 --> 00:00:09,616
(Leonard:)Genius here wants
to catch a bird

6
00:00:09,614 --> 00:00:11,284
(Leonard:)with a garbage bag
and a Slim Jim.

7
00:00:16,221 --> 00:00:19,291
(Raj:)Should have put it
in the bag first.

8
00:00:25,363 --> 00:00:27,733
(Penny:)So, if you don't
mind me asking,

9
00:00:27,732 --> 00:00:29,562
(Penny:)do you think you might
start dating again?

10
00:00:29,567 --> 00:00:31,397
(Dr Koothrappali:)It's much too soon for that.

11
00:00:31,402 --> 00:00:33,402
(Dr Koothrappali:)Why? Do you know someone?

12
00:00:33,404 --> 00:00:36,444
(Penny:)No, but if things don't
work out with me and Leonard,

13
00:00:36,441 --> 00:00:37,971
(Penny:)I'll give you a call.

14
00:00:37,976 --> 00:00:40,806
(Penny:)Wait. How much do you talk
about Star Trek?

15
00:00:42,413 --> 00:00:46,383
(Amy:)Okay, let's get this
Victorian party started.

16
00:00:46,384 --> 00:00:47,554
(Amy:)I've done some research

17
00:00:47,552 --> 00:00:49,822
(Amy:)about some traditional
parlor games we can play.

18
00:00:49,821 --> 00:00:51,121
(Penny:)Like what?

19
00:00:56,494 --> 00:00:57,614
(Amy:)Well, there's a fun one
called Ball of Wool.

20
00:00:57,611 --> 00:00:58,731
(Amy:)You take a ball of wool,

21
00:00:58,730 --> 00:01:01,400
(Amy:)and you put it right
in the center of the table.

